    {
      "@id": "#specimen-imaging-preparation-protocol-idr0118-keenan-flylightsheet-experimenta",
      "@type": "bia:SpecimenImagingPreparationProtocol",
      "name": "Specimen imaging preparation protocol",
      "description": "Virgin females maternally expressing Histone-GFP and MCP-mCherry (genotype: +;+;His-GFP/MCP-mCherry) were crossed to males with one of the endogenous transcriptional reporters (genotypes: +;+;tll-ms2/tll-ms2, +;+;hkb-ms2/hkb-ms2, +;+;byn-ms2/byn-ms2, +;+;fkh-ms2/fkh-ms2, or +;wg-ms2/wg-ms2;tll-ms2/+). An embryo from this cross was used in this experiment.\n\nNo treatment was performed on embryos\n\nEmbryos were imaged on a Luxendo MuVi SPIM light-sheet microscope, using 30x magnification setting on the Nikon 10x/0.3 water objective.  The 488 nm laser was used to image nuclei (His-GFP), and the 561 nm laser was used to image transcriptional dots (MCP-mCherry),  both at 5% laser power. Exposure time for the green channel was 55 ms and exposure for the red channel was 70 ms.  The line illumination tool was used to improve background levels and was set to 40 pixels. Image segmentation was performed for each 2D slice using a program called ilastik, which utilizes semantic segmentation. 3D object creation from 2D binary images and feature extraction was performed in a program called Arivis."
    },
